Caption: Discovery null controls (A03), blocks 1 to 6 of dinov2_vitb14_reg. (a) Twin fraction: the share of MLP hidden units in a matched pair whose symmetrised mirror correlation is at least 0.5. (b) Ratio to null of the share of weight energy the structure's projection removes: filled markers are the split-half ratio (operators fitted on one half of the fit images, pairings on the other), the statistic rule A03-1 scores, with a thin line across its two split directions; light open markers are the same-sample ratio, a diagnostic that sits below 1 for any fitted structure. C4 is the null itself (mean and 2.5 to 97.5 percentiles over its 20 draws). Dashed lines: the pre-registered bars (each control passes with a twin fraction of at most 0.05 and a ratio of at least 0.9). Rule A03-1: FAIL.

